### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Check a connection's status
#### composio ->>> GET /connected_accounts/{id} — status: INITIATED/ACTIVE/FAILED/EXPIRED/INACTIVE +
#### status_reason.
#### but we have: GET /connections/{id} only — smaller state machine (pending/active/revoked/error, no
#### distinct EXPIRED/auto-timeout — see research/execution-models.md's Composio comparison note). Secrets
#### always redacted.
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/connections/{{gmail_connection_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###
GET {{base_url}}/connections/{{serpapi_connection_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 List a user's connections (~ Composio's GET /connected_accounts, filtered to `user_id`)
#### Client-facing "which connections have I created" — NOT an admin "list every connection across every
#### user" view, that's GET /admin/users below. Optional &app=gmail to filter to one app.
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/connections?user_id={{user_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###
GET {{base_url}}/connections?user_id={{user_id}}&app=gmail
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Remove a connection (~ Composio's DELETE /connected_accounts/{id}) — real revoke, not cosmetic:
#### flips status -> "revoked" and clears `secrets`. `user_id` required, checked against the connection's
#### own owner. Doesn't delete the row (action_logs/trigger_instances still FK to it). Full per-app
#### examples: test_components/gmail/gmail.http and test_components/slack/slack.http.
### ----------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{base_url}}/connections/{{serpapi_connection_id}}?user_id={{user_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 List available apps (~ Composio's GET /toolkits) — the entry point: pick an app_slug here, then
#### narrow GET /actions below with it. Lightweight — no actions/schemas inlined, just counts.
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/apps
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 List / search tools (~ Composio's GET /tools). No more bare GET /actions — it now 400s unless you
#### pass ?q=<term> and/or ?app_slug=<app> (from GET /apps above), same complaint as Composio's own
#### "don't dump every tool across every toolkit" flow.
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/actions?app_slug=gmail
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

###
GET {{base_url}}/actions?q=recent
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Get one tool's real schema (~ Composio's GET /tools/{slug})
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/actions/GMAIL_LIST_RECENT_EMAILS
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Full OpenAPI surface — GET /apps + GET /actions above now cover the toolkit/tool-list views
#### Composio splits across GET /toolkits, /toolkits/{slug}, /tools?toolkit_slug=..., /tools/enum.
#### GET /openapi.json still works too, and DOES list every real action with its live schema
#### (generated, not hand-written). GET /triggers below covers the trigger side the same way.
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/openapi.json
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Example action — Gmail: send_email. Full Gmail action list: test_components/gmail/gmail.http
#### composio ->>> POST /tools/execute/{TOOL_SLUG} { user_id, connected_account_id, arguments, version }
#### — user_id AND connected_account_id both required, Composio composes them server-side.
#### but we have: POST /actions/execute/{tool_slug} { connection_id, input } — connection_id alone implies
#### both the user and the app. tool_slug is the same flat shape as Composio's (GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL).
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/actions/execute/GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{gmail_connection_id}}",
  "input": {
    "to": "someone@example.com",
    "subject": "Hello from tool_provider.http",
    "body": "Testing the action pipeline."
  }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Example action — Slack: post_message. Full Slack action list: test_components/slack/slack.http
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/actions/execute/SLACK_POST_MESSAGE
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "input": { "channel": "#test-user", "text": "Hello from tool_provider.http" }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Example action — Slack: get_channel_history (receive/read messages from #test-user). `channel_id` —
### conversations.history requires the real ID, unlike post_message's `channel` (which accepts a "#name").
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/actions/execute/SLACK_GET_CHANNEL_HISTORY
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "input": { "channel_id": "C0772SYKNN4", "limit": 20 }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Example action — SerpApi: search (SerpApi's only action)
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/actions/execute/SERPAPI_SEARCH
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{serpapi_connection_id}}",
  "input": { "query": "site:github.com composio" }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Triggers — list available (Gmail: new_email, new_labeled_email, new_sent_email, new_starred_email,
### new_draft. Slack: new_message.) Full per-app subscribe/unsubscribe flow: test_components/gmail/gmail.http
### and test_components/slack/slack.http.
#### composio ->>> GET /triggers_types (per-toolkit, requires x-api-key even for schema-only info).
#### but we have: GET /triggers, derived live from the registry (same "generated, not hand-maintained"
#### idea as /openapi.json's action schemas) — same ACCESS_TOKEN gate as everything else. Each entry
#### includes default_poll_interval_ms — NOT a global setting, see src/types.ts's TriggerDefinition
#### comment. Each entry also includes `payload`: real JSON Schema (via z.toJSONSchema) of the `data`
#### object this trigger delivers to a subscriber's webhook_url — `null` for a trigger that hasn't
#### declared its schema yet (TriggerDefinition.payload is optional).
### ----------------------------------------------------
GET {{base_url}}/triggers
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Example trigger — subscribe (Gmail new_email). Rest of Gmail's triggers (new_labeled_email,
### new_sent_email, new_starred_email, new_draft): test_components/gmail/gmail.http.
#### composio ->>> POST /trigger_instances/{slug}/upsert { connected_account_id | user_id, trigger_config:
#### {interval, ...} } — per-trigger interval, NOT global. Event DELIVERY is a separate step: POST
#### /webhook_subscriptions { webhook_url, enabled_events[] }, one URL for the whole project, decoupled
#### from individual trigger creation.
#### but we have: ONE call does both — POST /triggers/:app/:trigger/subscribe { connection_id, webhook_url,
#### poll_interval_ms? }. No global interval either — each trigger declares its own default
#### (src/types.ts's TriggerDefinition.defaultPollIntervalMs), overridable per-subscription via
#### poll_interval_ms below. src/core/scheduler.ts POSTs new events to webhook_url with a Composio-style
#### envelope: {id, type: "<app>.<trigger_key>", metadata: {trigger_instance_id, connection_id, user_id, app, extra_metadata}, data, timestamp}.
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/triggers/gmail/new_email/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{gmail_connection_id}}",
  "webhook_url": "https://webhook.site/your-unique-url-here",
  "extra_metadata": { "note": "created from tool_provider.http" }
}

### Copy the returned trigger_instance_id here to unsubscribe below
@gmail_new_email_trigger_id = ti_REPLACE_ME

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Triggers — unsubscribe
#### composio ->>> DELETE /trigger_instances/manage/{triggerId}
### ----------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{base_url}}/triggers/{{gmail_new_email_trigger_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

